[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2870403447","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106209#issuecomment-2870403447","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106209","id":2870403447,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rFuF3","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-12T00:34:04Z","updated_at":"2025-05-12T00:34:04Z","body":"Honestly, I would just keep the original method just to avoid the compatibility breakage. It looks like `get_actions()` was const, but `_get_actions()` wasn't. I would just keep `_get_actions()` and continue exposing it to classDB, and have it just be a one line wrapper for `get_actions()` to avoid breaking compatibility in the first place. \r\n\r\nThe compatibility system is great for when we need it, but this case doesn't justify the extra bloat as avoiding the need for the compat system would be much shorter and more elegant. \r\n\r\nThe compat system works well for GDExtension, but it doesn't help with GDScript and I think it doesn't help with C# either which needs manual b